# The cable, spelled two ways: `cabled-archie` for a person who wants that
# route and no other, and 10.77.77.2 for anything that has to name the route
# it is taking. dmux enrolls the address rather than `archie`, because the
# alias in 05- picks the cable or tailscale by probe and never says which --
# a route dmux has labelled usb, answering over tailscale, would license
# remote Wez on a path §8.3 has no row for. wezterm's built-in ssh client has
# the same problem from its own side: it hands the route's address to a
# client that does not implement `Match exec` at all. See docs/ssh.md,
# "Addressing the two routes".
#
# BindAddress is what keeps the spelling honest. 10.77.77.1 exists only while
# the cable does, so with the cable out this fails to bind rather than
# quietly resolving somewhere else -- the same reason 05- binds an address
# and not an interface name.
#
# Keepalives as tight as 05-, and for the same reason: the cable runs at
# ~1.7 ms with ±0.13 ms of jitter, so ten seconds of silence means it is gone
# and the session should say so rather than hang.

Host cabled-archie 10.77.77.2
    HostName 10.77.77.2
    User fredrir
    HostKeyAlias archie
    BindAddress 10.77.77.1
    ServerAliveInterval 5
    ServerAliveCountMax 2
